# Copy to `.env` in this same folder for local `npm run dev` use (a real
# `.env` already exists in this folder from earlier modules, with just
# VITE_API_BASE_URL set -- this file exists so the two NEW, Module 11
# variables below have a documented template too). Every variable here is
# read by Vite at BUILD time (`import.meta.env.VITE_...`) and baked
# directly into the compiled JavaScript -- see src/vite-env.d.ts and
# lessons/00-setup.md's "which .env, and when it's read" box.

# Already existed before this module. See ../backend/.env.example's
# sibling comment and module-09's lessons/08 for the empty-string,
# same-origin trick this project's Docker build uses in production.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Optional -- NEW in Module 11. Leave unset for local dev and every
# exercise -- src/monitoring.ts only calls Sentry.init(...) if this is
# actually set. Uses the SAME Sentry project as the backend's SENTRY_DSN
# (one project, two SDKs -- see lessons/06-monitoring-logging-and-error-tracking.md),
# but Sentry issues a DIFFERENT DSN string per platform, so don't reuse
# the backend's DSN value here.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0
# VITE_ENVIRONMENT=development
